  "id": "Compound::DB00321 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Amitriptyline is shown to interact with Cyp2b6 through a series of mechanistic pathways involving Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that Amitriptyline binds to Cyp2e1, which then participates in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, ultimately leading to Cyp2b6 being involved in this process. Similarly, Amitriptyline binds to Cyp2c19, which also participates in arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, and this pathway also leads to Cyp2b6. These findings indicate that Amitriptyline may modulate Cyp2b6 through shared enzymatic activities involving arachidonic acid epoxygenase. The consistent binding and participation scores across the three paths suggest a plausible, mechanistically linked relationship between Amitriptyline and Cyp2b6, particularly through the epoxygenase pathway. The evidence supports a role for Amitriptyline in influencing Cyp2b6 through the epoxygenase activity, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction and functional relevance.",
